    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1120-a2">

                <pb facs="1194" n="1098" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1098"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure to No. 2 in No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Dr. C. F. Gates to Mr. Straus.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bible House</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">O. S. Straus.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I find our steamer leaves at 4 p.m. to
                    morrow, the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Circassie</hi> of the Paquet Line.
                    Will you kindly see that a cavass is on hand by 3 o’clock to see that we are put
                    on board, and send necessary instructions to Samsoun.</p>
                <p>May I also suggest that when we are fairly started you should inform the Porte to
                    that effect and demand that instructions be sent all along our route that we be
                    not molested.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for all your kindness and regretting the trouble I have unwillingly
                    caused you,</p>
                <p>I remain, yours, truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Gates</hi>,</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
